TTYCHATTER.NCURSES(1)      User Commands      TTYCHATTER.NCURSES(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.ncurses - full-screen ncurses OpenRouter chat client

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.ncurses [session]
    ttychatter.ncurses --demo [session]
    ttychatter.ncurses --resume SESSION_OR_LOG
    ttychatter.ncurses --models
    ttychatter.ncurses --routers
    ttychatter.ncurses --test-model MODEL
    ttychatter.ncurses --doctor
    ttychatter.ncurses --version
    ttychatter.ncurses --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.ncurses is the full-screen terminal interface for ttychatter.
    It is OpenRouter-first and is intended to provide a browser-free chat
    client with sessions, model browsing, favorites, attachments, themes,
    diagnostics, GPG-aware API-key storage, and mouse/key-driven terminal UI.

USAGE
    Start in normal mode:
        ttychatter.ncurses

    Test without network chat calls:
        ttychatter.ncurses --demo

    Resume a session by name, .log filename, or path:
        ttychatter.ncurses --resume notes
        ttychatter.ncurses --resume notes.log
        ttychatter.ncurses --resume ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/notes.log

CONTROLS
    F1      Help / command menu
    F2      Model browser
    F3      API-key manager
    F4      Session browser
    F5      Options
    F6      Memory
    F7      Files / attachments
    F8      Open configured external editor for the current prompt
    F9      Credits
    F10     Quit

    Enter       Sends or inserts a newline depending on SEND_INPUT.
    Ctrl+G      Sends if SEND_INPUT is ctrl_g; remains a reliable send key.
    Ctrl+K      Quick attach file for the next message.
    Ctrl+L      List files currently queued for the next message.
    j/k         Move down/up in menu and list screens.

COMMAND AND HOTKEY BARS
    The main screen separates two kinds of controls.

    Function-key bar:
        Shows screen-navigation commands such as F1 Help, F2 Models,
        F5 Options, and F8 Editor.

    Compose hotkey bar:
        Shows actions that operate on the message currently being written,
        including the configured send key, Ctrl+K attachment, and Ctrl+L
        pending-file review.

    The send label reflects the current SEND_INPUT setting instead of always
    saying Enter or Ctrl+G.

API KEY STORAGE
    The F3 API-key screen supports three practical storage modes:

        runtime only
            The key is active only for the current run.

        encrypt with gpg
            The API-key entry screen shows a tickable "encrypt with gpg"
            option.  If gpg is installed, ticking this option stores the key in
            API_KEY_GPG_FILE using the external gpg command.

        plaintext config
            If the GPG checkbox is not ticked and the user chooses to save,
            ttychatter warns that the key will be stored in plaintext.

    If gpg is not installed, the API-key screen and options screen indicate:

        gpg not found

    Environment variables remain preferred for unattended use:

        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY

CONFIGURATION
    Default config file:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config

    Important keys:
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
        THEME
        SEND_INPUT
        MODEL
        MODEL_TYPE_FILTER
        MODEL_SORT_ORDER
        CONTEXT_TURNS
        SESSION_DIR
        ATTACHMENT_DIR
        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES
        CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND
        EDITOR

GPG NOTES
    GPG support is optional. ttychatter uses the external gpg command instead
    of implementing cryptography internally. The decrypted API key is never
    printed in diagnostics, logs, or transcripts.

EDITOR BEHAVIOR
    F8 opens the configured external editor immediately for the current prompt.
    The edited text is loaded back into the input pane after the editor exits.

    Editor selection belongs in F5 Options. The EDITOR option opens a detected
    editor selector that searches PATH, shows runnable editors, supports a
    custom command/path, and supports browsing for an executable.

MODEL BROWSER
    The F2 model browser supports cached OpenRouter model lists, search,
    sorting, favorites/bookmarks, router/fixed/free/auto filters, and explicit
    user-controlled network refresh.

FILES
    Sessions:
        ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/

    Attachments:
        ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments/

    Model cache:
        ~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json

    GPG API key:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/api-key.gpg

VERSION
    ttychatter.ncurses version 0.14.4
